question:
The CRO of an Indian bank is choosing a VaR method for a single INR-denominated commodity exposure. She sets three requirements:

- the VaR must be able to exceed the largest loss in the bank’s two-year historical sample when current conditions warrant;
- the method must use the GARCH volatility forecasts the bank already produces;
- every historical day must be used exactly once with an equal probability weight, with no resampling.

Which approach best meets all three requirements?

